 would skip `typescript`/`@types/*` and break `next build`.\\n\\n### Change #8: Keep host artifacts out of the build context\\n**File:** `services/frontend/.dockerignore`\\n**Action:** Use the **Write** tool (new file) with exactly this content. Without this, a stray host `node_modules` or `.next` would be copied by `COPY . .` and can break the in-container build with platform-mismatched binaries.\\n**Content:**\\n```\\nnode_modules\\n.next\\nout\\nnpm-debug.log*\\n.git\\n.DS_Store\\n```\\n\\n### Change #9: Keep build output out of git\\n**File:** `services/frontend/.gitignore`\\n**Action:** Use the **Write** tool (new file) with exactly this content.\\n**Content:**\\n```\\nnode_modules/\\n.next/\\nout/\\n*.tsbuildinfo\\n```\\n\\n## Constraints Recap\\n- Only the nine files above, all under `services/frontend/`, may be created.\\n- Do **not** modify `tests/integration/frontend-home.spec.ts`, `tests/playwright.config.ts`, `tests/package.json`, the root `docker-compose.yaml`, `docs/architecture/architecture.yaml`, or anything under `docs/`, `tests/`, or `true-bdd/`.\\n- Do **not** weaken, skip, or remove any assertion. The `h1` text must be produced by the app, not by relaxing the matcher.\\n\\n## Expected Result\\n`docker compose up --build frontend` builds `services/frontend`, starts `next start` on `0.0.0.0:3000` inside the container, compose publishes it on the host port derived in `tests/playwright.config.ts` via `FRONTEND_PORT`, Playwright's `webServer.url` poll succeeds (so `<startup>` passes), and `home page greets with Hello world` finds the single `h1` with text `Hello world`.\",\"questions\":[]}","structured_output":{"fix_prompt":"# Fix Prompt for Failing Test /playwright/playwright:<startup>\n\n## Root Cause\n\nThe test subject is the Playwright **`<startup>`** pseudo-test, i.e. the `webServer` block in `tests/playwright.config.ts` never came up, so no spec could run.\n\n- `tests/playwright.config.ts` starts the server with `docker compose up --build frontend` from the repo root and waits on `http://127.0.0.1:${port}`.\n- The repo-root `docker-compose.yaml` declares `frontend` with `build.context: ./services/frontend` and maps `\"${FRONTEND_PORT:-3000}:3000\"` (so the app must listen on **0.0.0.0:3000 inside the container**).\n- **`services/` does not exist at all.** There is no `services/frontend` directory, so `docker compose up --build frontend` fails immediately with an unreadable build context and startup times out.\n- The only spec, `tests/integration/frontend-home.spec.ts`, then asserts `page.goto('/')` renders a single `h1` whose text is exactly `Hello world`.\n\nThe fix is therefore to scaffold the missing production service: a minimal Next.js (App Router) + React + TypeScript app at `services/frontend/`, containerized so `docker compose up --build frontend` serves `/` on port 3000 with `<h1>Hello world</h1>`.\n\n`docker-compose.yaml` at the repo root is already correct — **do not touch it**, and do not touch anything under `tests/` or `docs/`. Every file below is new and lives under `services/frontend/`.\n\n## Required Changes\n\n### Change #1: Create the service package manifest\n**File:** `services/frontend/package.json`\n**Action:** Use the **Write** tool (new file) with exactly this content.\n**Content:**\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"frontend\",\n  \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"next dev -H 0.0.0.0 -p 3000\",\n    \"build\": \"next build\",\n    \"start\": \"next start -H 0.0.0.0 -p 3000\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"next\": \"^15.1.6\",\n    \"react\": \"^19.0.0\",\n    \"react-dom\": \"^19.0.0\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@types/node\": \"^22.10.0\",\n    \"@types/react\": \"^19.0.0\",\n    \"@types/react-dom\": \"^19.0.0\",\n    \"typescript\": \"^5.7.3\"\n  }\n}\n```\nNotes for the applier: do **not** hand-write a `package-lock.json`; the Dockerfile below uses `npm install`. The `-H 0.0.0.0 -p 3000` flags are required — the container port published by compose is `3000`, and binding to loopback only would make the published port unreachable from the host.\n\n### Change #2: Create the TypeScript config\n**File:** `services/frontend/tsconfig.json`\n**Action:** Use the **Write** tool (new file) with exactly this content. (The architecture quality gate declares this exact path at `architecture.services[frontend].quality_gate.code[typescript].config`, so the filename must match.)\n**Content:**\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2017\",\n    \"lib\": [\"dom\", \"dom.iterable\", \"esnext\"],\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"strict\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true,\n    \"esModuleInterop\": true,\n    \"module\": \"esnext\",\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"resolveJsonModule\": true,\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"preserve\",\n    \"incremental\": true,\n    \"plugins\": [{ \"name\": \"next\" }],\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\"./*\"]\n    }\n  },\n  \"include\": [\"next-env.d.ts\", \"**/*.ts\", \"**/*.tsx\", \".next/types/**/*.ts\"],\n  \"exclude\": [\"node_modules\"]\n}\n```\n\n### Change #3: Create the Next.js ambient type references\n**File:** `services/frontend/next-env.d.ts`\n**Action:** Use the **Write** tool (new file) with exactly this content.\n**Content:**\n```ts\n/// <reference types=\"next\" />\n/// <reference types=\"next/image-types/global\" />\n```\n\n### Change #4: Create the Next.js config\n**File:** `services/frontend/next.config.mjs`\n**Action:** Use the **Write** tool (new file) with exactly this content.\n**Content:**\n```js\n/** @type {import('next').NextConfig} */\nconst nextConfig = {};\n\nexport default nextConfig;\n```\n\n### Change #5: Create the App Router root layout\n**File:** `services/frontend/app/layout.tsx`\n**Action:** Use the **Write** tool (new file) with exactly this content. This is a server component (no `'use client'`), per the `component-composition` pattern in `docs/architecture/architecture.yaml` (\"Use server components by default\").\n**Content:**\n```tsx\nimport type { Metadata } from 'next';\nimport type { ReactNode } from 'react';\n\nexport const metadata: Metadata = {\n  title: 'Frontend',\n  description: 'Frontend service',\n};\n\nexport default function RootLayout({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {\n  return (\n    <html lang=\"en\">\n      <body>{children}</body>\n    </html>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Change #6: Create the home page that satisfies the assertion\n**File:** `services/frontend/app/page.tsx`\n**Action:** Use the **Write** tool (new file) with exactly this content. The page must render **exactly one** `h1` whose text content is exactly `Hello world` — `page.locator('h1')` is strict-mode and `toHaveText('Hello world')` compares the full normalized text, so do not add extra `h1` elements, suffixes, punctuation, or emoji.\n**Content:**\n```tsx\nexport default function HomePage() {\n  return (\n    <main>\n      <h1>Hello world</h1>\n    </main>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Change #7: Create the Dockerfile that compose builds\n**File:** `services/frontend/Dockerfile`\n**Action:** Use the **Write** tool (new file) with exactly this content. The root `docker-compose.yaml` uses `build.context: ./services/frontend` with no `dockerfile:` key, so it must be named exactly `Dockerfile` at the root of that context.\n**Content:**\n```dockerfile\nFROM node:22-alpine\n\nWORKDIR /app\n\nENV NEXT_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1\n\n# Install dependencies first so the layer caches across source edits.\n# devDependencies are needed: `next build` type-checks with typescript.\nCOPY package.json ./\nRUN npm install\n\nCOPY . .\n\nRUN npm run build\n\nEXPOSE 3000\n\nCMD [\"npm\", \"run\", \"start\"]\n```\nNotes for the applier: do **not** set `NODE_ENV=production` before `npm install` — that would skip `typescript`/`@types/*` and break `next build`.\n\n### Change #8: Keep host artifacts out of the build context\n**File:** `services/frontend/.dockerignore`\n**Action:** Use the **Write** tool (new file) with exactly this content. Without this, a stray host `node_modules` or `.next` would be copied by `COPY . .` and can break the in-container build with platform-mismatched binaries.\n**Content:**\n```\nnode_modules\n.next\nout\nnpm-debug.log*\n.git\n.DS_Store\n```\n\n### Change #9: Keep build output out of git\n**File:** `services/frontend/.gitignore`\n**Action:** Use the **Write** tool (new file) with exactly this content.\n**Content:**\n```\nnode_modules/\n.next/\nout/\n*.tsbuildinfo\n```\n\n## Constraints Recap\n- Only the nine files above, all under `services/frontend/`, may be created.\n- Do **not** modify `tests/integration/frontend-home.spec.ts`, `tests/playwright.config.ts`, `tests/package.json`, the root `docker-compose.yaml`, `docs/architecture/architecture.yaml`, or anything under `docs/`, `tests/`, or `true-bdd/`.\n- Do **not** weaken, skip, or remove any assertion. The `h1` text must be produced by the app, not by relaxing the matcher.\n\n## Expected Result\n`docker compose up --build frontend` builds `services/frontend`, starts `next start` on `0.0.0.0:3000` inside the container, compose publishes it on the host port derived in `tests/playwright.config.ts` via `FRONTEND_PORT`, Playwright's `webServer.url` poll succeeds (so `<startup>` passes), and `home page greets with Hello world` finds the single `h1` with text `Hello world`.","questions":[]},"ttft_ms":1605,"type":"result","duration_ms":112809,"uuid":"104f7f87-6f90-4947-bb4e-a91cf9e810fb","ttft_stream_ms":1015,"time_to_request_ms":39,"first_content_frame_ms":1015,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
